WEBVTT

00:00:00.058 --> 00:00:03.226
Two in three pressed 450 volts.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:06.601
In Milgram's obedience
study, volunteers had to

00:00:06.611 --> 00:00:09.286
shock a learner for every wrong answer,

00:00:09.311 --> 00:00:11.681
fifteen volts higher each time.

00:00:11.691 --> 00:00:13.106
They didn't know the learner was an

00:00:13.116 --> 00:00:15.680
actor, and the shocks were fake.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.342
A man in a grey lab coat

00:00:17.352 --> 00:00:19.140
told them to keep going.

00:00:19.202 --> 00:00:21.635
Sixty-five percent went all the way.

00:00:21.645 --> 00:00:23.945
Then Milgram changed just one thing.

00:00:23.995 --> 00:00:26.884
Same lab, same actor, same switches.

00:00:26.894 --> 00:00:28.134
The man in the coat left the

00:00:28.144 --> 00:00:31.182
room, and gave every order by phone.

00:00:31.192 --> 00:00:33.207
Full obedience fell to about one in

00:00:33.217 --> 00:00:34.232
five.

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:36.670
And many secretly gave weaker shocks than

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.667
ordered.
